From: MiniHub Contributors
Subject: esp-matter: null-check peer before CHIPoBLE GATT write

After GAP disconnect, peer_delete() removes the peer, but CHIPoBLE may still
call SendWriteRequest (e.g. StandAloneAck). SubscribeCharacteristic already
null-checks peer; SendWriteRequest did not and crashed in peer_svc_find_uuid.

Tree: ../esp-matter (connectedhomeip)
File: connectedhomeip/connectedhomeip/src/platform/ESP32/nimble/BLEManagerImpl.cpp
Apply-Root: ../esp-matter

Apply: ./tools/apply_component_patches.sh
---
--- a/connectedhomeip/connectedhomeip/src/platform/ESP32/nimble/BLEManagerImpl.cpp
+++ b/connectedhomeip/connectedhomeip/src/platform/ESP32/nimble/BLEManagerImpl.cpp
@@ -633,6 +633,12 @@ CHIP_ERROR BLEManagerImpl::SendWriteRequest(BLE_CONNECTION_OBJECT conId, const C
     const struct peer_chr * chr;
     int rc;
     const struct peer * peer = peer_find(conId);
+    // After GAP disconnect peer_delete() runs, but CHIPoBLE may still try StandAloneAck.
+    if (peer == nullptr)
+    {
+        ChipLogError(Ble, "Peer not found for CHIPoBLE write (conn may be closed)");
+        return BLE_ERROR_GATT_WRITE_FAILED;
+    }
 
     chr = peer_chr_find_uuid(peer, (ble_uuid_t *) (&ShortUUID_CHIPoBLEService), (ble_uuid_t *) (&UUID128_CHIPoBLEChar_RX));
     if (chr == nullptr)
